## Two rules that outrank convenience

1. **One set of facts, several representations.** Anything that appears in
   more than one place — an operation name, a log field, a Makefile target, a
   config key — has exactly one authoring location and is generated or checked
   everywhere else. A hand-written description that has drifted from the code
   is worse than no description.
2. **Guarantees are mechanical, not aspirational.** "Keep these in step" is
   not a rule; a check that exits non-zero when they diverge is. Add the check
   in the same change as the rule.

